    - Option 3 – Dual Constraint Relaxation with Intensive Monitoring (Least Preferred): Raise FatigueIndex ceiling to 0.50 and Noise ceiling to 85.0 dB concurrently. Requires mandatory 20-minute rest breaks every 90 minutes, continuous biometric fatigue monitoring with auto-pause on individual FatigueIndex > 0.52, full PPE mandate, and a post-sprint occupational-health review within 48 hours. This option closes the largest share of the demand gap but carries the highest worker-welfare risk and must be explicitly authorised by both the Production Manager and the site Health & Safety Officer before activation.
