    - Option 2 (Moderate): Deploy Engineering Controls and Ergonomic Rotation Protocol: Install acoustic dampening panels and hearing-protection dispensers at high-noise stations (targeting a 4–6 dB reduction) and implement a mandatory operator rotation schedule to cap continuous exposure per worker. Simultaneously introduce micro-break intervals calibrated to reduce fatigue accumulation rate. With effective noise engineering, Noise may be reduced to ~81.0 dB (still 1 dB above the 80.0 dB limit, requiring a minor temporary waiver); FatigueIndex can be managed to approximately 0.42 through rotation cadence. Partial constraint relaxation is required on both metrics. Estimated implementation: 5–10 business days. A ~12% deadline gap is expected during control installation.
