    - Option 3 (Last Resort): Supervised Temporary Constraint Waiver with Enhanced Monitoring: Formally waive FatigueIndex and Noise constraints to temporary elevated limits (FatigueIndex <= 0.50, Noise <= 85.0 dB) for a defined period not to exceed 14 calendar days. This option allows the current schedule to execute immediately and closes the deadline gap entirely, but it requires written authorization from the production manager and safety officer, mandatory real-time biometric and noise monitoring, and a post-period health audit for all affected workers. Regulatory disclosure may be required depending on jurisdiction. This option carries the highest occupational health risk and must be treated as a controlled exception, not a standing policy. All constraint relaxations must be logged in the CBPA audit trail.
