    - Option 3 (Last Resort): Supervised temporary relaxation of FatigueIndex with mandatory compensatory protocols: With explicit written authorisation from the production manager and occupational-health oversight, temporarily raise the FatigueIndex ceiling to 0.50 and mandate documented compensatory rest periods after every elevated-exposure shift. Concurrently deploy engineering noise-reduction controls (acoustic enclosures, upgraded PPE) targeting in-shift Noise below 82 dB. This option meets the demand deadline without a gap but introduces elevated occupational health risk. A formal risk-acceptance record must be filed, the relaxation is time-boxed to 30 days, and a root-cause capacity review must be completed before the period expires. Human-centric constraints are intentionally breached and are therefore not preserved.
