    - Option 3 (Last Resort) — Time-Limited Constraint Relaxation with Compensatory Controls: Temporarily raise the operational FatigueIndex ceiling to 0.50 and the Noise ceiling to 83.0 dB for a capped window not to exceed 72 consecutive hours. Compensatory controls are mandatory: 20-minute paid rest breaks every 90 minutes, Class B hearing-protection PPE for all personnel, and daily occupational-health check-ins. This option closes approximately 12% of the deadline gap but explicitly violates the original human-centric thresholds and requires formal written authorisation from the production manager and the occupational-health officer before activation. It must not be used without logging an exception in the CBPA governance audit trail.
